; The root delegates two zones, and the first one's name server is a
; name inside the second.
;
; ns.sibling. is below the sibling. delegation, so the root carries an
; address for it: that is the glue sibling. needs.  The same record is
; then the only address available for example., whose NS RRset names
; that very host.  For example. it is not glue at all in the strict
; sense -- it is not below example. -- but it is the parent's to hand
; over, and a resolver has to decide what it is worth.
$ORIGIN .
$TTL 3600
@		IN	SOA	ns.root. root.root. 1 3600 900 604800 3600
@		IN	NS	ns.root.
ns.root.	IN	A	{{ROOT_ADDR}}
example.	IN	NS	ns.sibling.
example.	IN	DS	{{DS example}}
sibling.	IN	NS	ns.sibling.
ns.sibling.	IN	{{AUTH_ADDR_RR}}
sibling.	IN	DS	{{DS sibling}}
